      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DOCUMENT-PROFILE-AND-AI-EXECUTION-MODELS.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="entity-operations" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/entity-operations.md">Create payload shapes.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-18; read the To Do and document-save code listed above; re-grep every caller of `CreateDocumentWithSpePointersAsync` and `ApplyAssociationLookup`.</step>
    <step order="1">Write failing tests first: Office document save under a Matter carries the association, I-1 stamp, owner (BU default Owner team, or the carried OwningTeamId) and search index in the CREATE, and exactly one create call is made with no association update; Office To Do goes through the service with the caller principal; redelivered finalization message creates no second document.</step>
    <step order="2">Convert `CreateTodoAsync`: pass user-entered values and regarding carriers to the service; delete its private owner resolution and creator-person stamp once the registry covers them (task 012/013 handle creator person); keep the response `CreateTodoResponse` and endpoint codes.</step>
    <step order="3">Convert document save (persistence class and worker) to one service create carrying the association columns; determine which SPE pointer fields (drive/item ids, hash) are known at create and pass those; if a pointer update must remain, keep it as a pointer-only update and record the evidence.</step>
    <step order="4">Preserve the carried-OwningTeamId rule as an explicit service input; preserve content-duplicate detection and the worker's retry semantics.</step>
    <step order="5">Build; run Office contract tests, the OfficeVersionSave data-mutation tests, OfficeRecordOwnershipTests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests unchanged; publish-size delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the association cannot be set in the create because Dataverse rejects the bind before the SPE pointers exist (a required pointer column), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the exact error; do not reintroduce an association-only follow-up update.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the UploadFinalizationWorker cannot obtain a scoped service per message without a DI change, STOP and escalate (ADR-010) before adding any registration.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep `_documentService.CreateDocumentAsync` / `UpdateDocumentAsync` in Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs (~:283, ~:330) and Workers/Office/UploadFinalizationWorker.cs (~:636, ~:687), and `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync` in OfficeService.cs (~:2289). Existing tests: tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeSaveDocumentStampContractTests.cs and OfficeTodo*ContractTests.cs cover stamp and regarding authorization, not the association-in-create invariant.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for production code: both paths call the existing service; no new production file. The only new file is a test class, because the association-in-create/one-call assertion belongs to no existing suite and the existing contract tests must pass unchanged.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>An Office-created document under a Matter is created without the association, so it misses mapping, I-1 stamp, owner and search index at create and relies on a follow-up update that can fail between the two calls (spec FR-18 acceptance, word gaps G1/G2).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs (To Do)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Workers/Office/UploadFinalizationWorker.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/OfficeDocumentCreateAssociationTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An Office-saved document under a Matter carries its association, mapping (if a profile exists), I-1 stamp, record-first owner and search-index default in the create; no separate association update is issued (asserted by a call-count test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/office/todo` creates through `RecordCreationService` with the caller principal; `OfficeService.CreateTodoAsync` no longer calls `_genericEntityService.CreateAsync` for `sprk_todo`; the response and error codes are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A carried `OwningTeamId` on the finalization payload still wins as the owner (email attachment children match their parent), asserted by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A redelivered upload-finalization message does not create a second document (existing duplicate detection still the guard).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an Office To Do naming a regarding record the caller cannot AppendTo is refused with the existing uniform outcome and no row is created; a refused or failed service call in the worker creates no document and takes the existing error path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; Office contract tests (OfficeTodo*, OfficeSaveDocumentStamp*, OfficeQuickCreate*), OfficeVersionSave data-mutation tests, OfficeRecordOwnershipTests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests* and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests pass unchanged; publish-size delta and CVE result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-18. Office Invoice quick-create was done in task 018. If document save keeps a pointer-only update, the determination and evidence are recorded in the task notes, and the live check is task 036.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
